// A module's identity is what its 'mod' declaration names it, not its filename.
//
// Two modules are imported. moduledeclared.cone declares 'mod renamed', so the
// name this file binds for it is 'renamed' and its filename is not a name here at
// all; modulesub.cone declares no module, so it keeps the name its filename gave
// it. That second half is transitional and stays only until the folder walk
// replaces filename naming altogether.
//
// cases.toml pins that both halves reach the declaring module's own symbols, and
// that nothing is spelled after the filename of the module that renamed itself.
//
// It compiles rather than runs: it spans modules.
//
// The imported modules are moduledeclared.cone and modulesub.cone.

import moduledeclared;
import modulesub;

fn viaDeclaredName() i64 {
  renamed.scaleBy(3i64) + renamed.timesFactor() + renamed.factor;
}

fn viaFileName() i64 {
  modulesub.plain(2i64);
}
